  "evidence": "SwissWatchExpo 59363 original specimen. All 12 original gallery images inspected 17 November 2026; movement 8 reviewed at 1200px from original 2470px file. Visible 3135 bridge stamp and numeric 31 rotor inscription. Case engraving 6 reads 16610 T; listing identifies base 16610. T recorded as observed case marking, not a new alias or universal transition date. Black dial and elapsed-time bezel, date loupe and steel-coloured Oyster/flip-lock visible. Dealer attributes 2005–2006, 40mm steel case and sapphire crystal; these remain attributions. No LV or later ceramic execution transfer. No transfer to neighbouring references or other unopened specimens; original fitment, service status, full chronology and user-watch authenticity are not independently established. Existing photographs remain separate specimens. Overall execution/period research remains incomplete.",
